{
  "kanda": "bala",
  "sarga": 68,
  "title": "Janaka sends word to Ayodhya",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga68/balasans68.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga68/balaitrans68.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Janaka's delegation arrives at Ayodhya and submits its message to Dasharatha. Listening to the tidings that his son Rama not only lifted the bow of Shiva, but broke it as well, Dasharatha is overjoyed and refers the matter of marriage of Seetha with Rama to his ministers and teachers. All of the ministers and sages unanimously agree to that proposal and they are set to travel to Mithila the next day."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकिरामायणे आदिकाव्ये बालकाण्डे अष्टषष्टितमः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 68th chapter in Bala Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1.68.1",
      "label": "1.68.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "जनकेन समादिष्टा दूतास्ते क्लान्तवाहनाः |\nत्रिरात्रमुषिताः मार्गे तेऽयोध्यां प्राविशन् पुरीम्",
      "iast": "janakena samādiṣṭā dūtāḥ te klānta vāhanāḥ |\ntri rātram uṣitā mārge te ayodhyām prāviśan purīm",
