    {
      "id": "1.68.8",
      "label": "1.68.8",
      "numbers": [
        8
      ],
      "devanagari": "सेयं मम सुता राजन् विश्वामित्रपुरस्कृतैः |\nयदृच्छयागतैर्वीरैर्निर्जिता तव पुत्रकैः",
      "iast": "sā iyam mama sutā rājan viśvāmitra puraskṛtaiḥ |\nyadṛcchayā āgataiḥ vīraiḥ nirjitā tava putrakaiḥ",
      "translation": "\"Oh, Emperor Dasharatha, your young and valorous son who serendipitously arrived at Mithila along with his younger brother Lakshmana, keeping Vishvamitra at his fore, finally carries off this girl, the well-known daughter of mine...",
      "notes": [
        "Usually this verse gives meaning that 'two of your valorous sons won Seetha...' because of the usage of plural number <em>vīraiḥ putrakaiḥ</em> But this is counted as 'royal we' sort of expression to honour Rama. Hence this <em>ka pratyaya</em>, though used in the verse, will be read as singular. There is another shade of wording for this verse: <em>seyam mama sutā rājan viśvāmitrsya śāśanāt | purīm imām samāgatya tava pureṇa nirjitā ||</em> which uses only singular for Rama."
      ],
