    {
      "id": "1.68.16",
      "label": "1.68.16",
      "numbers": [
        16
      ],
      "devanagari": "दृष्टवीर्यस्तु काकुत्स्थो जनकेन महात्मना |\nसंप्रदानं सुतायास्तु राघवे कर्तुमिच्छति",
      "iast": "dṛṣṭa vīryaḥ tu kākutstho janakena mahātmanā |\nsampradānam sutāyāḥ tu rāghave kartum icchati",
      "translation": "\"On observing the valour of Kakutstha Rama, noble souled Janaka wishes to gift his daughter as bride to Raghava Rama...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "kaakutsthaH",
          "iast": "kākutsthaḥ",
          "devanagari": "काकुत्स्थः",
          "meaning": "of Kakutstha Rama - on his part",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mahaatmanaa janakena dR^iSTa viiryaH",
          "iast": "mahātmanā janakena dṛṣṭa vīryaḥ",
          "devanagari": "महात्मना जनकेन दृष्ट वीर्यः",
          "meaning": "by noble-souled, by Janaka, one whose valour has been observed [on observing Rama's valour]",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sutaayaaH sampradaanam",
          "iast": "sutāyāḥ sampradānam",
          "devanagari": "सुतायाः सम्प्रदानं",
          "meaning": "of daughter, gift of bride",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raaghave kartum icChati",
          "iast": "rāghave kartum icchati",
          "devanagari": "राघवे कर्तुं इच्छति",
          "meaning": "in respect of Raghava, to do, he wishes.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.68.17",
      "label": "1.68.17",
      "numbers": [
        17
      ],
      "devanagari": "यदि वो रोचते वृत्तं जनकस्य महात्मनः |\nपुरीं गच्छामहे शीघ्रं मा भूत्कालस्य पर्ययः",
      "iast": "yadi vo rocate vṛttam janakasya mahātmanaḥ |\npurīm gacchāmahe śīghram mā bhūt kālasya paryayaḥ",
      "translation": "\"If you all favour the tidings from the noble-souled Janaka as to what has happened in Mithila, we quickly proceed to that city, let not the time lapse...\" Thus Dasharatha informed his counsel.",
      "notes": [
        "The word <em>vṛttam</em> 'happening' 'history' and it is generally translated as 'the history, legend, and the familial characteristics of Janaka...' But when Janaka already is famous through the bow of Shiva, and that bow itself is broken now, no more 'verification of antecedents' of Janaka is needed, and it is 'what has happened now' i.e., the impossible deed of breaking it."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "mahaatmanaH janakasya vR^ittam",
          "iast": "mahātmanaḥ janakasya vṛttam",
          "devanagari": "महात्मनः जनकस्य वृत्तं",
          "meaning": "noble-souled, Janaka's, what has happened to - surprised assent to give daughter",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaH rocate yadi",
          "iast": "vaḥ rocate yadi",
          "devanagari": "वः रोचते यदि",
          "meaning": "to you, interested, if",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shiighram puriim gacChaamahe",
          "iast": "śīghram purīm gacchāmahe",
          "devanagari": "शीघ्रं पुरीं गच्छामहे",
          "meaning": "quickly, to city [Mithila,] we proceed",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 6
